    "done_when": "Evidence 2026-09-26 ~20:43-20:46Z: during an engine relaunch under a router pause, three clive launches exited code 2 before any stream record with 'clive: global catalog is unreachable: HTTP Error 503: Service Unavailable' (reckon runs r-20260926T204258990000, r-20260926T204338144105, and imas-ambix r-20260926T204600683610) - the router answers /v1/models 503 while no engine is reachable. In imas_ambix/agent/clive.py, the launcher's catalog read (fetch_catalog / cached_catalog, failing at the 'global catalog is unreachable' branch near line 334) retries a 503 or 502 response and a refused or reset connection with bounded exponential backoff (start ~2 s, cap ~30 s) for a total bound of 900 s, printing one stderr line per retry naming the status and remaining budget, and fails as today only when the bound is exhausted or the error is not one of those; a 404 or malformed catalog still fails at once. Tests in a new tests/test_agent_clive_catalog_retry.py exercise the generated launcher program against a local HTTP stub: 503 twice then the real catalog (proceeds), 503 until a short test-scaled bound (fails with the unreachable message), 404 (fails at once). 'uv run --no-sync pytest -p no:cacheprovider tests/test_agent_clive_picker.py tests/test_agent_clive_worker_profile.py tests/test_agent_clive_catalog_retry.py' exits 0 on the login node; 'uv run --no-sync ruff check imas_ambix tests' exits 0; negative control recorded verbatim with its failing count at a committed revision. Do not regenerate or overwrite the installed launcher under /work/projects/imas_gpu/agents/ (the coordinator deploys). Landing: one short paragraph in plan §17; no evidence section, no figure. Pass checkout_path on every reckon MCP call; never write or run git in the main checkout.",
